{
  format: 1
  name: genesis-required-singleton-member-unpopulated-rejects
  suite: static
  spec: ["#loading", "§9.1", "#state-model", "§5.1", "#mutations", "§8.2", "#runtime", "§22.1"]
  note: '''
    §22.1 lists "field and shape types" among the STATE CONSTRAINTS, which "hold
    in every committed state" — the very first one included. §8.2 makes a writable
    non-collection root member durable state at its own address, and §5.1 gives a
    field a value at insertion either from the caller or from a declared default.
    `none` is absence rather than a value (§5.5, Annex A.1), so a NON-optional
    root member with no default and no `$seed`/`$bundle` value has no admissible
    committed state at all: genesis must refuse it.

    §9.1 fixes the discipline: seed data "passes through the same defaults,
    normalization, checks, key, ref, uniqueness, bucket, and meter rules as
    mutation inserts", so genesis is judged by the same population rule every
    later state is. The refusal is FAIL-CLOSED AT CREATION — an instance created
    with a member that no committed state can satisfy would otherwise be
    unmigratable, since the same rule refuses it on the first update (§20.1
    checks the complete prospective target) and blames a migration that changed
    nothing.

    `theme` is bundled so the instance holds root state and the reserved row
    exists; `motto` is the required member left unpopulated. The sibling case
    `genesis-optional-singleton-member-absent-admits` pins the other side: an
    OPTIONAL member holding nothing is admissible, so the rejection is about the
    declared shape and not about absence itself.
  '''

  package: {
    $liasse: 1
    $app: "t.reqsing@1.0.0"
    $model: {
      motto: "text"
      theme: "text?"
      settings: { $view: ". { motto, theme }" }
    }
    $bundle: { theme: "T1" }
  }

  expect: {
    outcome: rejected
    violates: ["#runtime", "§22.1", "#state-model", "§5.1", "#loading", "§9.1"]
    detail: "the root member `motto` is declared `text` (non-optional) with no default and no `$seed`/`$bundle` value, so the genesis state would leave it unpopulated"
  }
}
